bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    interp_private_names_selfhost_check_2026-11-09, 0, "2026-11-09 lane-p2-1 BLOCKED-EVIDENCE. Insertion point identified: module_import_resolution.spl named-import loop (after surface_declares_item_indexed) can reject a ModuleSurfaceCallable with is_public=false from a different-directory, non-test/** importer, mirroring seed check_private_use_names (module_loader.rs:616) + is_test_caller. Blockers: (a) 20.hir has no file I/O and no project-root handle, so the 20181-pair scripts/check/private_import_baseline.txt must be loaded by the driver and transported into HirLowering (new field + driver wiring); (b) native builds lower SCV snapshot paths (build/scv/snapshots/<rev>/...), so the repo-relative baseline key must strip that prefix or every baselined legacy pair becomes a hard error and the self-hosted bootstrap breaks; (c) proving (b) needs a stage2 rebuild + native closure build, not possible with C: at 4-8 GB free. Without (a)+(b) the check is a guess patch with bootstrap-break risk."

